WEBVTT

00:35.114 --> 00:38.084
<i>We now return to
America's Next Top Model.</i>

00:38.134 --> 00:40.536
I just don't think
you're being fair, Tyra.

00:40.550 --> 00:43.503
You don't know what it's like
to grow up the way I grew up.

00:43.504 --> 00:47.224
You know what? How dare you?!
You don't know me.

00:47.257 --> 00:51.158
You have no idea where
I come from, where I've been,

00:51.191 --> 00:53.311
how long I've been there,

00:53.347 --> 00:58.845
what I had to do to get from
where I was to where I am now!

01:05.785 --> 01:07.824
- Hey there, Mort.
- Hi, Lois.

01:07.845 --> 01:10.660
Neil's doing a report
on Christianity at school.

01:10.672 --> 01:13.101
Do you have any crucifixes I can borrow?

01:13.117 --> 01:15.356
Preferably one without
the little fellow on it?

01:15.367 --> 01:17.962
Oh, of course, there's one
in the den. Help yourself.

01:19.680 --> 01:22.431
God, I'm sick of Mort
always borrowing our stuff.

01:22.447 --> 01:25.049
He's a bigger mooch than
the Mexican Super Friends.

01:31.558 --> 01:34.410
Hey, Mexican Superman,
can I talk to you for a sec?

01:34.425 --> 01:36.605
When you signed the lease,
you said there was going to be like

01:36.619 --> 01:37.797
five of you living here.

01:37.823 --> 01:41.015
Oh, no, they're not all living here.
They're just visiting.

01:44.075 --> 01:47.469
Hey, Mexican Superman,
I got the keys made.

01:47.483 --> 01:49.555
Hey, Mexican Batman, get out of here.

01:49.571 --> 01:52.359
- What? I got like 60 keys.
- Silйncio!

01:52.375 --> 01:53.782
- Jefe aquн!
- їQuй?

01:53.817 --> 01:55.177
Eviciуn.

01:58.540 --> 02:00.481
That ought to keep Mort away.

02:00.506 --> 02:02.202
Peter, what the hell is that?

02:02.217 --> 02:04.468
Lois, I'm tired of Mort
always mooching off us,

02:04.484 --> 02:05.699
so I made a scare-Jew.

02:05.716 --> 02:08.239
Peter, we're not gonna have
this in our front yard.

02:08.263 --> 02:11.453
It's racist, and for God's sake,
you ruined your best suit.

02:11.478 --> 02:13.159
Now we're gonna have
to get you a new one...

02:13.164 --> 02:14.652
Shh. Lois Lois, look.

02:14.757 --> 02:17.297
Hey, guys, I just wanted
to return your...

02:17.301 --> 02:20.435
Oh! Oh, my God, it's Hitler! He's back!

02:20.471 --> 02:22.779
He's back! Hurry, protect Jon Stewart!

02:22.807 --> 02:24.918
He's our most important Jew!

02:28.489 --> 02:30.198
Why do wo get me a suit here?

02:30.213 --> 02:33.826
Well, since you keep ruining them, I'm
not going to buy you a brand-new one.

02:34.672 --> 02:37.974
Yes, I'll take this teddy bear,
this ruler,

02:38.000 --> 02:41.594
this piece of string and
this cardboard box.

02:44.929 --> 02:47.738
Oh, look, an "On The Raggedy Ann" doll.

02:47.956 --> 02:50.356
<i>It's water weight, you bastard!</i>

02:50.389 --> 02:52.659
<i>Get off me! I'm not your whore.</i>

02:53.484 --> 02:56.330
<i>I'm sorry, I'm just so sad.</i>

02:56.343 --> 02:59.223
Well, I guess I can still play with it
three weeks out of the month.

02:59.892 --> 03:02.914
- Hi, there. See anything you like?
- Oh, I'm just browsing.

03:02.948 --> 03:05.842
Say, you look like you
could use an activity book

03:05.857 --> 03:07.664
with half the activities done.

03:08.162 --> 03:11.194
- That would save me half the time.
- Connect the dots?

03:11.219 --> 03:14.299
Ha! More like set the book down
and have a beer.

03:14.324 --> 03:16.073
You got yourself a deal.

03:20.177 --> 03:22.487
What... are those?!

03:22.523 --> 03:25.205
Oh, that's a pair of
red flannel feety pajamas.

03:25.222 --> 03:26.157
Good Lord.

03:26.192 --> 03:28.674
See, they've got a flap
that opens up in the back.

03:28.698 --> 03:31.360
Are you telling me I could be
pooping and warm?

03:31.384 --> 03:32.504
Exactly.

03:32.527 --> 03:35.688
No longer would I have to make
a choice between the two.

03:35.785 --> 03:38.186
Sir, here is a check with my name on it.

03:38.209 --> 03:41.361
Write down any number on
this piece of paper, and I will pay it.

03:45.507 --> 03:46.864
All right, so we roll the dice

03:46.880 --> 03:49.192
and then we both have to yell
"Yahtzee" really loud.

03:49.217 --> 03:50.233
- At the same time?
- Yeah.

03:50.238 --> 03:52.018
And you have to flap
your wrists like this.

03:52.022 --> 03:52.969
And you'll do it, too?

03:52.982 --> 03:54.682
- Of course, that's how it's done.
- Okay.

03:54.698 --> 03:56.496
- All right, ready?
- Okay, you gonna do with me?

03:56.511 --> 03:57.211
Oh, yeah.

03:57.757 --> 03:59.063
Yahtzee!

03:59.089 --> 04:00.266
- Gay.
- You suck!

04:00.343 --> 04:02.190
Hey, everybody, I'm home from work.

04:02.214 --> 04:05.228
My God, Peter, you wore
those pajamas to your office?

04:05.241 --> 04:06.923
Hey, at least
I'm mixing it up a little bit.

04:06.938 --> 04:09.456
Green shirt, tan pants,
that's refreshing.

04:09.525 --> 04:12.565
Oh, boy does it feel good
to undo my butt flap.

04:12.601 --> 04:15.993
Ew, Dad! We don't want to
sit here and look at your ass.

04:16.028 --> 04:18.819
Yes, I'd rather look at Meg
toweling off after a shower

04:18.822 --> 04:20.794
when she does that butt floss thing.

04:21.712 --> 04:23.378
Ew, ew, that's so disgusting.

04:23.393 --> 04:26.195
Ugh, ugh, I hope I don't ever
accidentally use that towel.

04:27.074 --> 04:29.422
Lois, I have never been more comfortable

04:29.440 --> 04:31.727
as a person than I am
in these feety pajamas.

04:31.754 --> 04:33.223
All warm and furry.

04:33.288 --> 04:35.205
This is what it feels like to be a bear.

04:35.220 --> 04:37.523
You remember what I used to say,
Lois, when we first got married?

04:37.536 --> 04:39.910
You remember? I used to say :
"What would it feel like to be a bear?"

04:40.285 --> 04:42.002
Well, this is it. This is it.

04:42.157 --> 04:44.377
- I'm living it, baby.
- No, you're not.

04:44.402 --> 04:46.533
You've been wearing
those things for three days.

04:46.538 --> 04:49.208
You can wear them to bed, but
tomorrow we're getting rid of them.

04:49.693 --> 04:50.611
Fine.

04:50.629 --> 04:52.547
Screw up all my fuzziness.

04:55.370 --> 04:57.380
What the hell was that?

04:58.465 --> 04:59.523
Oh, my God.

04:59.900 --> 05:01.667
Lois, don't get alarmed, but

05:01.905 --> 05:03.672
I think I might be Jesus.

05:04.038 --> 05:05.065
I'm Jesus.

05:05.102 --> 05:06.680
Peter, that's a static shock.

05:06.694 --> 05:09.013
Your pajamas created
a charge of electricity

05:09.041 --> 05:10.770
when you dragged your feet
across the carpet,

05:10.796 --> 05:12.763
and when you touched Chris,
you passed it on.

05:12.787 --> 05:14.339
Kneel before Christ!

05:25.216 --> 05:26.013
Dad!

05:26.041 --> 05:27.388
I am not your dad.

05:27.853 --> 05:29.894
I am Electric Man.

05:39.381 --> 05:40.890
Damn it, Peter, stop it!

05:40.903 --> 05:42.333
I got to tell you, you're pissing me off

05:42.348 --> 05:45.118
worse than when I watched the
O.J. verdict with my old roommate.

05:45.274 --> 05:49.128
<i>We the jury find the defendant
Orenthal James Simpson,</i>

05:49.142 --> 05:50.281
<i>not guilty...</i>

05:50.304 --> 05:51.544
- Yes!
- What the hell?!

05:51.989 --> 05:52.858
- What?!
- What?!

05:54.013 --> 05:57.026
- Maybe we should get new roommates.
- Yeah, maybe we should.

06:00.156 --> 06:01.137
Peter.

06:01.189 --> 06:02.748
I know you're in here.

06:02.765 --> 06:04.251
Yes, I am, Lois.

06:04.791 --> 06:06.708
But where?

06:06.735 --> 06:09.905
Peter, if you shock me,
I swear to God I'm leaving you.

06:09.933 --> 06:11.951
You'll have to find me first, Lois.

06:11.963 --> 06:13.676
Where could I be?

06:13.690 --> 06:17.033
Well, there's a Quonset hut that
I've never seen in this room before.

06:17.068 --> 06:19.526
- I got to figure you're in there.
- How do you know, Lois?

06:19.545 --> 06:22.594
I could be in that New York
style magazine kiosk.

06:22.609 --> 06:24.980
Peter, this all looks very expensive.

06:25.006 --> 06:27.134
Yes, you might say it was...

06:27.162 --> 06:29.069
shockingly expensive.

06:29.096 --> 06:31.005
I'm going to try the Quonset hut.

06:31.912 --> 06:33.239
I was in the bathroom.

06:33.255 --> 06:36.677
The hut and the kiosk...
decoys, Lois, decoys!

06:40.261 --> 06:43.796
Glen, thank you so much
for helping me tear up my carpet.

06:43.821 --> 06:45.760
Well, you know, Lois, I got to confess,

06:45.785 --> 06:48.525
when you called me I sort of
misunderstood what you were asking for.

06:48.539 --> 06:50.130
That's why I rushed over.
But, uh...

06:50.153 --> 06:52.945
Well, it's fine, it's fine,
whatever, I'm happy to help.

06:52.973 --> 06:54.599
What the hell is this?

06:54.614 --> 06:56.655
Peter, I've had it with
all your shocking.

06:56.679 --> 06:59.860
Since you won't get rid of those
pajamas, I'm getting rid of the carpets.

06:59.885 --> 07:02.097
Hey, Lois, you want me to leave
a little strip in this thing?

07:02.111 --> 07:04.553
Maybe a lightning bolt, unicorn,
something like that?

07:04.578 --> 07:08.362
- No, I want it all gone, Glen.
- All right, we're going Brazilian.

07:09.159 --> 07:10.375
Hey, what's this?

07:10.409 --> 07:13.158
- Some kind of really old coin.
- Huh. Let me see that.

07:13.340 --> 07:15.334
Wait a minute, do you know what this is?

07:15.356 --> 07:17.964
This is an 18th-century
Rhode Island ship token.

07:17.980 --> 07:19.755
This thing's got to be worth 50 grand.

07:19.782 --> 07:22.232
50 grand?! Oh, my God!

07:22.250 --> 07:24.135
I can finally afford that operation

07:24.153 --> 07:26.623
to swap my vocal cords
with Patrick Stewart.

07:26.758 --> 07:31.144
Hey, Lois, I spent the afternoon
making a list of famous Armenians.

07:31.199 --> 07:34.052
Eric Bogosian, Andre Agassi,

07:34.128 --> 07:36.385
Jerry "The Shark" Tarkanian.

07:36.469 --> 07:37.668
That is all.

07:40.492 --> 07:43.551
Peter, you've been sleeping
with that money for the past week.

07:43.579 --> 07:45.806
Don't you think it's time
we did something with it?

07:45.822 --> 07:47.703
Buy a bolt and shut that trap of yours?

07:47.717 --> 07:48.505
- What?
- What?

07:48.519 --> 07:49.916
'Cause I had an idea.

07:49.931 --> 07:51.351
Remember when we first got married...

07:51.366 --> 07:53.234
And I said, "I wonder what it
would be like to be a bear"?

07:53.249 --> 07:56.360
No, no, no, I'm talking about
that dream we had, Peter.

07:56.388 --> 07:58.949
Remember? We tried
to open that restaurant,

07:58.964 --> 08:00.904
and we never quite got it going.

08:00.918 --> 08:03.858
Yeah, we got shut down
'cause of my exploding cupcakes.

08:03.934 --> 08:06.898
Mmm, I hope these taste
as good as they look.

08:08.284 --> 08:09.725
Gerald!

08:10.560 --> 08:12.618
The secret is in the frosting.

08:12.633 --> 08:14.806
But I'll never tell.

08:14.870 --> 08:17.994
Well, here's another chance
to open a restaurant.

08:18.018 --> 08:19.195
You're right.

08:19.220 --> 08:21.521
- And I'll make my special cupcakes.
- No, Peter...

08:21.533 --> 08:23.324
Oh, yeah, right, that was the problem.

08:27.701 --> 08:30.201
All right, everybody,
only three hours till opening.

08:30.227 --> 08:32.755
Oh, this is going to be
the coolest place in Quahog.

08:32.773 --> 08:35.823
All the movers and shakers
and bigwigs are going to eat here...

08:35.848 --> 08:38.050
but not the small wigs.

08:38.095 --> 08:40.422
Hey, I'm hungry.

08:40.461 --> 08:42.338
I got a credit card.

08:42.363 --> 08:45.625
Oh, God, I'm so nervous.
I hope it goes well.

08:45.651 --> 08:49.274
Oh, yes, I'm sure it will go as well
as Liza Minnelli's Playboy shoot.

08:49.530 --> 08:52.009
Oh, God, please put
your clothes back on.

08:52.035 --> 08:53.974
Mama... Mama...

08:54.442 --> 08:56.310
Do you love me now, Mama?

08:56.906 --> 08:59.007
Please love me, Mama!

09:03.163 --> 09:05.572
Good evening. Welcome to
Big Pete's House of Munch.

09:05.606 --> 09:08.508
- May I help you?
- Yes, do you accept the Discover card?

09:08.953 --> 09:11.786
Hey, Lois, Diamond Jim Brady over here

09:11.801 --> 09:14.333
just asked if we accept
the Discover card.

09:15.060 --> 09:18.294
They're in an exclusive club
called anybody.

09:18.326 --> 09:20.658
Yeah.
No, no, no, I don't think so.

09:20.753 --> 09:23.996
You know, you know,
I would rather take two live chickens

09:24.008 --> 09:26.069
than your fly-by-night credit card.

09:26.256 --> 09:28.896
I would rather take a jar of pennies

09:28.913 --> 09:31.420
that's value was less
than that of your bill.

09:31.435 --> 09:33.527
- Look, you don't have to insult me.
- No, no, no.

09:33.540 --> 09:36.493
You are going to sit there
and listen to the funny things

09:36.508 --> 09:38.578
I would take instead
of your credit card.

09:40.559 --> 09:44.864
The guy at table 7 complained there's
not enough juice on his prime rib.

09:44.887 --> 09:46.125
Oh, did he, now?

09:46.150 --> 09:47.929
Let me take care of that for him.

09:51.201 --> 09:53.514
Tell him, bon appйtit, douchebag.

09:56.124 --> 09:58.596
Oh, look, it's one of those
early Maude episodes

09:58.608 --> 10:00.749
with the really long opening
credit sequence.

10:04.042 --> 10:07.486
<i>Lady Godiva was a freedom rider</i>

10:07.531 --> 10:10.584
<i>She didn't care if
the whole world looked</i>

10:10.787 --> 10:14.423
<i>Joan of Arc with the Lord to guide her</i>

10:14.518 --> 10:17.179
<i>She was a sister who really cooked</i>

10:17.824 --> 10:21.427
<i>Madame Curie was a
strong woman character</i>

10:21.451 --> 10:24.666
<i>Working all day in a science lab, yeah</i>

10:24.781 --> 10:27.974
<i>Clara Barton was a famous nurse</i>

10:27.998 --> 10:31.331
<i>Who was rapping with
the soldiers and bandages, too</i>

10:31.664 --> 10:35.400
<i>Susan B. Anthony always out doin' stuff</i>

10:35.423 --> 10:38.288
<i>Marching around and holding up signs...</i>

10:38.299 --> 10:39.440
<i>And then there's Maude.</i>

10:39.466 --> 10:42.607
<i>- Pocahontas had it all goin' on
- What the hell?</i>

10:42.650 --> 10:46.063
<i>An Indian guide
with lots of Indian pride</i>

10:46.161 --> 10:49.731
<i>Indira Gandhi ran a whole big country</i>

10:49.789 --> 10:52.831
<i>That isn't easy even if you're a guy...</i>

10:52.853 --> 10:54.264
And then there's Maude?

10:54.309 --> 10:57.561
<i>- Babe Zaharias was a really good athlete
- Aw, come on!</i>

10:57.595 --> 11:00.557
<i>Good at track and field
and professional golf, too</i>

11:00.573 --> 11:01.870
And then there's Maude!

11:01.914 --> 11:05.328
<i>Amelia Earhart flew a lot of airplanes</i>

11:05.373 --> 11:08.656
<i>Except for that one time
when she didn't come back</i>

11:08.701 --> 11:12.425
<i>- Cleopatra lived way out in the desert
- And then there's Maude! Come on!</i>

11:12.459 --> 11:15.842
<i>But still found a way
to keep herself looking fine</i>

11:16.429 --> 11:18.411
<i>And then there's Maude...</i>

11:19.576 --> 11:20.863
There we go!

11:20.899 --> 11:22.461
That was an ordeal.

11:22.553 --> 11:25.065
Well, Peter, this has been
an amazing week.

11:25.090 --> 11:28.284
You and I own a restaurant.
Can you believe it?

11:28.298 --> 11:30.075
I know. I feel like I'm dreaming.

11:30.090 --> 11:30.817
Wait.

11:30.835 --> 11:32.430
Maybe I am dreaming.

11:32.455 --> 11:35.521
That means I can do whatever
I want without consequences.

11:37.890 --> 11:39.346
What are you doing?

11:39.375 --> 11:41.544
I just adopted 30 puppies!

11:56.344 --> 11:58.282
You guys, I have some bad news.

11:58.287 --> 11:59.836
I just finished going over the books,

11:59.852 --> 12:02.060
and this restaurant is
hemorrhaging money.

12:02.064 --> 12:04.555
What? Well, how is that possible?

12:04.571 --> 12:06.863
Isn't it obvious?
We're not getting enough customers.

12:06.878 --> 12:09.057
This place is like a
ghost town half the time.

12:09.071 --> 12:11.271
Yeah. Maybe somebody
should have asked me.

12:11.286 --> 12:14.550
After all, I'm the only one in this
family with any business experience.

12:14.603 --> 12:16.204
All right, Violet and Pigpen,

12:16.210 --> 12:18.988
you've been seeing each other a few
weeks now. What seems to be the problem?

12:18.995 --> 12:21.895
I keep getting bladder infections,
and I don't know why.

12:21.942 --> 12:23.058
Really?

12:23.095 --> 12:24.672
You don't know why?

12:27.666 --> 12:29.152
I don't know what to do, guys.

12:29.157 --> 12:31.339
The House of Munch is
going down the tubes.

12:31.352 --> 12:34.306
Maybe you need to do
a little advertising, Peter.

12:34.332 --> 12:35.307
Well, I tried.

12:35.312 --> 12:38.423
I even hired M. Night Shyamalan
to direct my TV commercial.

12:38.769 --> 12:40.912
I have a secret to tell you.

12:41.026 --> 12:43.003
- What is it?
- Come closer.

12:43.620 --> 12:46.984
I see good food at competitive prices.

12:47.258 --> 12:49.983
At Big Pete's House of Munch!
Stop on by!

12:50.046 --> 12:51.623
Unfortunately, they couldn't air it,

12:51.631 --> 12:54.630
'cause it turns out M. Night Shyamalan
was involved with September 11.

12:54.658 --> 12:58.309
You know, Peter, my buddies and I
have been looking for a new hangout.

12:58.337 --> 13:01.127
Our usual doughnut shop
has gotten a little...

13:01.204 --> 13:02.889
Puerto Ricany.

13:02.915 --> 13:05.777
What if we made your place our new spot?

13:05.791 --> 13:07.652
Joe, that's a great idea!

13:07.666 --> 13:09.707
Fantastic! We'll see you tonight.

13:09.732 --> 13:11.048
This is awesome!

13:11.083 --> 13:14.259
Bunch of cops in uniform
hanging out in my restaurant?

13:14.274 --> 13:15.899
This is going to be cooler
than that time

13:15.915 --> 13:18.144
Ben Stiller taught me how to be myself.

13:18.541 --> 13:21.302
But how can you leave me now,
Ben Stiller,

13:21.330 --> 13:23.240
when I need you more than ever?

13:23.253 --> 13:25.944
I've taught you everything
you need to know, Peter.

13:25.961 --> 13:28.409
Now it's time for me
to go help another child.

13:28.445 --> 13:32.469
I guess I just fooled myself into
thinking you'd always be with me.

13:32.485 --> 13:33.744
I will, Peter.

13:33.817 --> 13:35.957
I will always be with you.

13:45.092 --> 13:47.556
His movies are terrible...

13:52.651 --> 13:56.103
Lois, roll out the red carpet.
Here comes Joe and his cop buddies.

13:56.128 --> 13:58.239
You got tables for 30?

14:02.205 --> 14:05.807
Whoa, whoa, whoa, Joe! I thought you
were bringing your cop friends over.

14:05.822 --> 14:07.791
What are all these
parallelograms doing here?

14:07.816 --> 14:10.899
You mean paraplegics.
These are my friends, Peter.

14:10.923 --> 14:12.544
Come on, guys. Let's eat.

14:12.709 --> 14:16.592
Oh, God. I hope there's not one of
those angry, handicapped Vietnam guys

14:16.607 --> 14:18.937
with the bandana on his head.
Oh! There he is.

14:18.952 --> 14:22.176
I've seen some things, man,
and some stuff.

14:22.239 --> 14:23.868
I wouldn't recommend it.

14:31.059 --> 14:34.413
Peter, isn't this wonderful?
The place is packed.

14:34.449 --> 14:36.176
Uh... Lois, uh...

14:36.282 --> 14:38.070
aren't you a little freaked out by this?

14:38.088 --> 14:40.558
Why? Everybody's having a great time.

14:40.573 --> 14:42.792
Besides, think of the
money we're making.

14:42.806 --> 14:45.368
I don't care about that.
I wanted a cool restaurant,

14:45.384 --> 14:47.783
not the cafeteria at the
veteran's hospital.

14:47.798 --> 14:50.551
This is weirder than that
rap video by M.C. Escher.

14:51.826 --> 14:53.757
<i>Going up the stairs
and going down the stairs</i>

14:53.803 --> 14:55.944
<i>And going up the stairs
and going down the stairs</i>

14:55.988 --> 14:58.196
<i>And going up the sideways stairs.</i>

15:00.810 --> 15:04.331
And, in local news, a new restaurant
is taking Quahog by storm.

15:04.347 --> 15:06.127
That's right, Diane.
If you're handicapped,

15:06.143 --> 15:09.364
or know someone who's handicapped, or
just happen to be a fan of the circus,

15:09.399 --> 15:11.750
then come on down
to Big Pete's House of Munch,

15:11.753 --> 15:14.083
where the elite without feet
meet to eat.

15:14.139 --> 15:17.260
Lois, this is insanity. I think we
should shut down the restaurant.

15:17.347 --> 15:19.907
But... why? We're doing so well.

15:19.943 --> 15:23.687
Lois, let me explain something to you,
all right? Cripples are not cool.

15:23.721 --> 15:26.412
- Hang on. I'm going to get the picture.
- Oh, Peter, don't...

15:28.161 --> 15:30.252
- What do you see here, Lois?
- Do we have to...?

15:30.265 --> 15:31.734
What do you see?!

15:32.262 --> 15:35.883
- A picture of Mark Harmon.
- A picture of Mark Harmon,

15:35.899 --> 15:38.089
the greatest actor who ever lived.

15:38.104 --> 15:39.996
Do you see a wheelchair
under Mark Harmon?

15:39.998 --> 15:41.076
- Peter...
- Lois,

15:41.603 --> 15:42.852
do you...

15:42.935 --> 15:44.787
see a wheelchair...

15:45.364 --> 15:47.181
under Mark Harmon?

15:47.245 --> 15:49.157
- No.
- No, you do not,

15:49.182 --> 15:51.251
because Mark Harmon is cool.

15:51.274 --> 15:54.750
I know what you're thinking. "Peter,
this is just like your Gil Gerard speech."

15:54.765 --> 15:57.404
And you can stop right in
your tracks, because it is not.

15:57.458 --> 16:00.120
Granted, it is similar to the
Gil Gerard speech, but it...

16:00.145 --> 16:02.435
Peter, I like our restaurant
the way it is,

16:02.460 --> 16:04.793
and if you don't, that's your problem.

16:05.155 --> 16:07.820
Fine. Then I'll deal with this myself.

16:10.609 --> 16:12.208
All right, here they come.

16:15.070 --> 16:17.391
Hey, Peter, we're here for dinner.

16:17.415 --> 16:20.217
Oh no, you're not, Joe.
We have a new policy.

16:20.245 --> 16:21.411
Can't you read the sign?

16:24.140 --> 16:26.133
Peter, what the hell is that all about?

16:26.166 --> 16:27.633
It's a message, Joe.

16:27.648 --> 16:30.200
I don't want you and your
kind eating here anymore.

16:30.224 --> 16:33.106
You're ruining what was supposed
to be a cool establishment.

16:33.122 --> 16:35.063
Peter, you're one of my closest friends.

16:35.085 --> 16:38.590
Are you... you telling me that you have
a problem with me being handicapped?

16:38.606 --> 16:41.275
As a matter of fact, Joe, yes.
I think it's immoral.

16:41.300 --> 16:43.953
It's a lifestyle choice
you're forcing on America.

16:43.986 --> 16:46.820
We handicapped are a proud people!

16:46.833 --> 16:49.393
Yeah, when you're not drinking and
gambling on your reservations,

16:49.410 --> 16:51.190
which we gave you.

16:51.225 --> 16:53.704
Fine, if that's the way you want it,

16:53.721 --> 16:56.179
but we're not going to go down easy.

16:56.988 --> 16:58.365
Okay, that was easy.

16:58.390 --> 17:01.071
But I'll be back with
more handicapped guys!

17:06.397 --> 17:08.671
Dad, look! Here they come!

17:13.485 --> 17:16.878
Peter, we'll give you
one last chance to let us in!

17:17.263 --> 17:19.865
What are you going to do, Joe?
I'm up here.

17:20.351 --> 17:23.363
And you're down there.

17:23.450 --> 17:26.288
Very well, Peter,
you leave us no choice.

17:26.407 --> 17:29.145
Men, form up Crippletron!

18:19.078 --> 18:22.150
Help! Help! Somebody help me!

18:23.617 --> 18:25.727
Ben Stiller, help me.

18:25.802 --> 18:28.485
No, Peter. I heard what
you said about my movies.

18:28.499 --> 18:29.447
How did you hear?

18:29.501 --> 18:30.570
Hello!

18:30.592 --> 18:33.398
Go to hell, you mutant offspring
of comedy people.

18:36.307 --> 18:39.288
Mrs. Griffin, I'm afraid
he'll never walk again...

18:39.475 --> 18:41.425
without remembering how lucky he is

18:41.439 --> 18:43.651
that he'll only be in this
wheelchair for two weeks.

18:43.663 --> 18:45.714
That leg should heal up just fine.

18:45.727 --> 18:49.080
Peter, you do realize you deserve this
for the way you treated Joe.

18:49.088 --> 18:51.177
I think you owe him an apology.

18:51.191 --> 18:52.239
Are you kidding, Lois?

18:52.253 --> 18:54.403
It ain't my fault that him
and all his gimpy friends

18:54.418 --> 18:56.278
don't fit in with regular society.

18:56.345 --> 18:57.611
But I'm going to be different.

18:57.638 --> 19:01.292
I'll be a dignified cripple,
and I'll show them all how it's done!

19:13.735 --> 19:15.674
<i>Don't wish it away</i>

19:16.048 --> 19:20.154
<i>Don't look at it like it's forever</i>

19:23.616 --> 19:26.039
<i>Between you and me</i>

19:27.133 --> 19:29.214
<i>I could honestly say</i>

19:29.542 --> 19:32.152
<i>That things can only get better</i>

19:35.555 --> 19:37.953
<i>And while I'm away</i>

19:40.275 --> 19:43.970
<i>Dust out the demons inside</i>

19:44.965 --> 19:49.952
<i>And it won't be long
before you and me run</i>

19:50.410 --> 19:52.989
<i>To the place in our hearts</i>

19:53.807 --> 19:56.106
<i>Where we hide</i>

19:59.399 --> 20:03.826
<i>And I guess that's why
they call it the blues</i>

20:08.519 --> 20:13.104
<i>And I guess that's why
they call it the blues.</i>

20:14.145 --> 20:15.251
Joe, uh...

20:15.437 --> 20:17.418
- you got a minute?
- What is it, Peter?

20:17.430 --> 20:18.350
I, uh...

20:18.402 --> 20:20.273
just wanted to apologize.

20:20.308 --> 20:23.482
I thought you and your friends
were just a bunch of gross cripples,

20:23.645 --> 20:26.729
but I've been in a wheelchair
for 45 minutes now,

20:26.742 --> 20:28.302
and I see how tough it is.

20:28.327 --> 20:31.537
Well, Peter, it's been a
rough week for both of us,

20:31.563 --> 20:34.508
but it means a lot to me
to hear you say that.

20:34.552 --> 20:37.180
So what do you say?
Can we put all this behind us?

20:37.218 --> 20:38.794
I'd like nothing better.

20:38.872 --> 20:42.623
Hey, Bonnie and I are watching
Grey's Anatomy if you want to come in.

20:42.650 --> 20:45.259
Oh, boy, Joe, I...
I got to tell you, that... that...

20:45.707 --> 20:47.137
that sounds awful.

20:47.138 --> 21:48.138
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru